  "findingSummary": "12-DOF quadratic plate warps over the 19 fit border ticks reduce fit-set single-coordinate RMS (7.684 to 2.680 km on equidistant conic), but degrade held-out edge ticks (3.729 to 7.629 km) and worsen interior Bactria landmark error (68.84 to 93.35 km equidistant; 63.18 to 169.30 km Lambert, where Pataliputra also degrades to 255.62 km). Shifting standard parallels [12N, 26N] to [10N, 28N] alters Pataliputra by only 0.27 km (57.69 to 57.42 km). The ~57-69 km interior offset is therefore intrinsic plate symbol/compilation tolerance, not edge page curl.",
